            <h1 class="jw-heading-130"><strong>Combat Aircraft Technology and New Developments</strong></h1>
<h2 class="jw-heading-100"><strong> Introduction</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>Overview of Advanced Fighter Aircraft Technology</li>
<li>Introduce new technology developments</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="jw-heading-100"><strong> Major Projects and Aircraft</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>The JSF/IST program</li>
<li>NexGen Air Battlespace</li>
<li>Notable Aircraft:
<ul>
<li>F-15EX Strike Eagle</li>
<li>F-16 Fighting Falcon (Viper) and variants</li>
<li>F-22 Raptor</li>
<li>F-35 Lightning II</li>
<li>Su-57 Felon</li>
<li>Shenyang FC-31 Gyrfalcon</li>
<li>KAI KF-21 Boramae</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="jw-heading-100"><strong> Emerging Technologies</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>Next-Generation Air Dominance (NGAD) Aircraft</li>
<li>Collaborative Combat Aircraft (CCA)</li>
<li>Advanced Electro-Optical Targeting System (EOTS)</li>
<li>Sensor and Data Fusion</li>
<li>Aircraft Datalink Systems</li>
<li>Artificial Intelligence Co-pilot</li>
<li>Energy Weapons (e.g., Lasers)</li>
<li>MicroElectro-Mechanical Systems (MEMS)</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="jw-heading-100"><strong>JAST/IST and JSF F-35 Program</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>Collaborative Competition</li>
<li>Integrated systems</li>
<li>Inclusion of designs that had already begun</li>
<li>Advanced technology:
<ul>
<li>Electro-Optical Targeting Systems (EOTS)</li>
<li>LiftFan and VTO/SL configuration</li>
<li>Very-Low Observable (VLO) profile</li>
<li>Electro-Hydrostatic actuators</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="jw-heading-100"><strong> Conclusion</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>Summary of Key Points Discussed</li>
<li>Future Outlook on Combat Aircraft Technology</li>
<li>Closing Remarks</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>    </div>
